    <sys:String x:Key="Str_ProtocolGuideTitle">ISO 8253-1 / ASHA Standard Threshold Guidelines</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_ProtocolGuide1">Utilizes standard 10-down / 5-up bracketing; 2-of-3 responses on ascending runs establishes threshold.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_ProtocolGuide2">Sequence: 1000 Hz → 2000 Hz → 4000 Hz → 8000 Hz → 1000 Hz (Retest) → 500 Hz → 250 Hz.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_ProtocolGuide3">Hard safety limit locked at 50 dB HL. No response after two 50 dB HL attempts is recorded as NR @ 50 dB HL.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_ProtocolGuide4">Random silent Catch Trials are inserted to quantify false-positive rates and guarantee reliability.</sys:String>

